WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:05.460
Welcome to Ear Biscuits, the podcast

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:06.990
where two lifelong friends talk

00:00:06.990 --> 00:00:09.860
about life for a long time, I'm Rhett.

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:10.800
And I'm Link.

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.670
This week at the round
table of dim lighting,

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.140
I'm talking about, I'm just gonna give you

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:19.563
a little bit of update
on my spiritual journey.

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.640
My spiritual walk.

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.610
How's my walk?

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:23.560
How's your walk, Rhett?

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.090
Well, I read my Bible last night,

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:25.923
you know it's-

00:00:25.923 --> 00:00:28.120
Just that's the thing
we used to ask people.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.820
It's like, that was kind of the shorthand

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:35.660
when we were in evangelicalism, be like,

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.230
how's your walk?

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:38.300
How's your walk with the Lord?

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:39.357
I never asked anybody that with that...

00:00:39.357 --> 00:00:41.900
How's your walk.
With that look on my face,

00:00:41.900 --> 00:00:42.733
or that accent.

00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:47.710
Or it would be like,
how's your quiet time?

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:49.583
Well, like I told you,

00:00:49.583 --> 00:00:50.950
I read my Bible last night.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.500
Actually, I got three pages into

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:55.404
the introduction of the study Bible

00:00:55.404 --> 00:00:56.790
and fell asleep.

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.950
The introduction is not
a part of the Bible.

00:00:59.950 --> 00:01:01.440
Well, it is this Bible.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:02.280
It's the study part,

00:01:02.280 --> 00:01:03.113
but it's not the Bible part.

00:01:03.113 --> 00:01:04.610
No, no, I was actually
looking at the back.

00:01:04.610 --> 00:01:08.053
I was reading the selling
points of the Bible,

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:13.310
and it was, it said 60% Bible, 40% notes.

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:14.200
I was like, okay.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.342
That's a good breakdown.

00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:16.370
60, 40?

00:01:16.370 --> 00:01:17.440
Yeah.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:21.010
So, you fell asleep in
the intro, that's a-

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.097
You know what?
That's a pretty thick intro.

00:01:22.097 --> 00:01:23.990
Isn't it? Just leave it at that, man.

00:01:23.990 --> 00:01:24.980
That's why I think I
can probably get three,

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.362
or four pages a night.

00:01:27.362 --> 00:01:29.010
I think there was 2,500 pages,

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:30.193
do the math on that.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:34.040
I'll be reading for 1,000 years.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.387
It's so interesting that like-

00:01:35.387 --> 00:01:36.450
A few years.

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:37.967
I think, here is one of the things

00:01:37.967 --> 00:01:40.770
that's gonna come clear over the course

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:44.860
of me kind giving the one year up update

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:49.418
of my quest in spirituality.

00:01:49.418 --> 00:01:50.730
Two year, I think.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:51.950
Well, one year from
the last time I did it.

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:52.943
Okay, annual.

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:55.453
You know you make that joke,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:58.200
and you're able to laugh at the fact

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:00.130
that like, hey, yeah, I'll take...

00:02:00.130 --> 00:02:01.710
I'll just take...

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.768
If I do it a couple of pages at a night,

00:02:03.768 --> 00:02:06.130
I'll make progress.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:08.170
And the way that I
would interact with that

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:11.780
and I don't know, it's
like I tense up inside,

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:14.700
and I'm like, I have...

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.640
'Cause you turn it into an obligation.

00:02:16.640 --> 00:02:18.830
Yeah, we can explore it more,

00:02:18.830 --> 00:02:21.030
but I'm just kind of laying it out there

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.120
at this point that, yeah, it's...

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:30.300
It's laying out another plan, or system,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:35.500
or idea against which to measure myself

00:02:35.650 --> 00:02:39.229
and beat myself up to fall short.

00:02:39.229 --> 00:02:40.062
Mm.

00:02:40.062 --> 00:02:42.060
It's the tendency that I have that I'm...

00:02:43.375 --> 00:02:47.500
That I described when I originally,

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.477
when I went back and looked at my journals

00:02:49.477 --> 00:02:51.600
for the first time we talked

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.160
about our spiritual deconstruction

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:54.810
and I had my episode.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:59.450
I'm reminded of reading
my college journals

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:04.150
and just how I just
felt sorry for that guy

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.620
because he was

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.380
just constantly beating himself up.

00:03:10.380 --> 00:03:13.010
And this is something
that I'm still coming

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.680
to grips with, I'll come back to it,

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:19.060
but the place I wanna
start is this past weekend.

00:03:19.060 --> 00:03:21.840
Just to kinda just give you an update,

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:24.420
which is in some ways related,

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:27.610
but some ways just a nice story

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:29.160
that I wanna tell you.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.830
You know this, you had plans this weekend,

00:03:31.830 --> 00:03:33.250
you were doing some...

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.270
You were going outta town, and I'm like,

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:37.410
well damn, I'm gonna make some plans too.

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:38.243
Mm-hmm.

00:03:38.243 --> 00:03:39.076
It's like okay-

00:03:39.076 --> 00:03:40.212
That's usually how it works.

00:03:40.212 --> 00:03:41.045
You gonna be gone Friday.

00:03:41.045 --> 00:03:43.650
you're gonna be gone Monday.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.990
So, I'm like, oh, this
is a great opportunity

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:49.860
for me, and I realized well in advance

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:54.763
that it was over the Valentine weekend.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:03:57.530
And I was like, this is actually clicking

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:01.130
into place because Lily and I have

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:05.050
this tradition every year to go out,

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:06.880
I take her out on a Valentine's date.

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:07.713
Mm-hmm.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:08.590
And one of the things I was thinking

00:04:08.590 --> 00:04:11.920
in terms of her being off at college,

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.420
her being a freshman is that this will be

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.480
the first year that we won't be

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:18.530
in the same place.

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:20.090
We're not gonna have the opportunity

00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:23.860
to keep our tradition alive.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:28.860
Unless, I drive and surprise her.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.833
Mm-hmm.

00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:31.853
And now that I have some extra time

00:04:31.853 --> 00:04:34.750
with this long weekend,
I was able to do that.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.525
And at first Christie was like, well,

00:04:37.525 --> 00:04:39.530
should we all go and surprise her?

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:41.170
She's talking about us coming up there

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.210
and seeing her.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:43.993
Nah, well, it just kinda needs

00:04:43.993 --> 00:04:46.250
to be just my thing, you know?

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:47.390
It's just like pouring milk.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:48.230
This is just...

00:04:48.230 --> 00:04:49.063
Important milk?

00:04:49.063 --> 00:04:50.660
It's just like pouring milk.

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:52.920
Oh, yeah, it's my thing.
This is your thing.

00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:54.160
Well, yeah, it's our date.

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:55.880
So, if we all surprised her,

00:04:55.880 --> 00:04:58.380
even if I just went on a date with her.

00:04:58.380 --> 00:05:01.360
Honestly, the other
thing I was thinking was

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.263
this'll be like a mini solo trip for me.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:09.103
I'll be on the road a lot,

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.780
and then I decided I'm
gonna rent a sprinter van.

00:05:12.780 --> 00:05:15.357
Yeah, baby, getting back
in that sprinter van,

00:05:15.357 --> 00:05:16.650
I'm gonna be camping.

00:05:16.650 --> 00:05:18.850
I don't know where I'm
gonna end up every night.

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:21.653
I'm just a rambler.

00:05:22.507 --> 00:05:26.690
I'm just a rolling stone and I just love

00:05:26.690 --> 00:05:27.523
the idea of it.

00:05:27.523 --> 00:05:29.760
So, I was hankering to hit the road.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.000
Like all those country
songs when it's like,

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.630
well, don't plan on me
being around for long,

00:05:34.630 --> 00:05:37.230
'cause I gotta wrap everything up

00:05:37.230 --> 00:05:40.099
in my bandana and get
back on the road, or-

00:05:40.099 --> 00:05:41.130
That's not...

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:41.963
That's not really...

00:05:41.963 --> 00:05:44.390
Yeah, is a little antithetical

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:45.493
to your personality.

00:05:45.493 --> 00:05:47.880
It's like, "I'm really ready to get home

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.380
and settle in."

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.213
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:50.213 --> 00:05:51.360
Well that's the thing about the van

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:54.270
is that you take everything with you

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.580
and no matter where you go,

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.330
you got everything that you've decided

00:05:58.330 --> 00:05:59.180
that you need.

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:00.013
Oh, yeah.

00:06:00.013 --> 00:06:04.510
Including your high priced blender

00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:06.790
and all of your smoothie ingredients.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.100
Oh, you can just hook up

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.540
a regular blender and 'cause

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:11.270
it has regular power.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:13.290
Yeah, man, it's got an inverter.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.210
It's got solar panels.

00:06:15.210 --> 00:06:16.778
It's got AC if you need it.

00:06:16.778 --> 00:06:18.468
It's got heat if you need it.

00:06:18.468 --> 00:06:19.301
So, you made a smoothie-

00:06:19.301 --> 00:06:20.349
It's got a shower-
Every morning.

00:06:20.349 --> 00:06:21.510
With a toilet in it.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:24.270
You could take a dump
while taking a shower

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:26.330
in the exact same place.

00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:27.293
I didn't do that.

00:06:29.084 --> 00:06:31.123
But you had a smoothie every day?

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:33.960
I skipped one day.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.860
It's good to give your body a break.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:37.673
Anyway.

00:06:38.636 --> 00:06:40.240
I thought it would be like

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.110
a nice mini solo trip too.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:46.960
This podcast was coming up.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:49.290
It would gimme some more
time for reflection.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:50.123
Mm-hmm.

00:06:50.123 --> 00:06:52.360
And processing.

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.470
I'm like, well I know
I'm a verbal processor,

00:06:54.470 --> 00:06:57.110
so I might be talking out loud to myself,

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.680
but no one will know.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.220
People driving by on the freeway

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.223
will think that I'm on a call,

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:05.233
if it comes to it.

00:07:11.976 --> 00:07:13.580
So, the surprise for Lily

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:17.090
was Christie ended up talking to her

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.890
about how she was shipping something

00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:21.280
to her dorm room.

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.660
So, she needed to be there on Saturday.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.190
We didn't know exactly
when it was gonna show up.

00:07:27.190 --> 00:07:29.460
So, she was basically trying to say,

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:31.190
don't make plans because
there's something here.

00:07:31.190 --> 00:07:32.760
And then I, when I talked to her,

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.390
I was like, we have this tradition.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.300
We're gonna have to do
it virtual this year

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.920
and mom's shipping something that you...

00:07:39.920 --> 00:07:42.600
Once you get that, then
we're gonna do our...

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:43.800
I have an idea, we're
gonna do a virtual thing.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.370
Was the shipping a lie?

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:46.350
It was a lie.

00:07:46.350 --> 00:07:47.183
Oh, wow.

00:07:47.183 --> 00:07:49.480
It was me that was showing up,

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.000
I was the package.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:54.170
Okay, well, a little deceptive.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:55.330
Well, yeah, I mean it's just

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:57.360
you can lie for a surprise.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:07:58.770
Yeah, I agree with that.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.990
You and your...

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:01.580
Are you a Bible thumper now?

00:08:01.580 --> 00:08:02.413
Yeah, yeah, I've been reading.

00:08:02.413 --> 00:08:03.880
I read three and a half
pages of the Bible-

00:08:03.880 --> 00:08:04.713
Yeah, you know-

00:08:04.713 --> 00:08:06.723
Last night and I gotta say, I'm...

00:08:06.723 --> 00:08:08.209
Lying's an issue with me now.

00:08:10.021 --> 00:08:11.620
The truth is very important to me.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:15.630
Yes, I know, Rhett.

00:08:15.630 --> 00:08:16.723
You and your truth.

00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:22.270
I'm a big fan of meaning though.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.972
Maybe I'll get back to
that, talk about that.

00:08:23.972 --> 00:08:25.510
Okay, okay.

00:08:25.510 --> 00:08:28.250
So, actually I got there Friday night,

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:30.150
she got out of a class,

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:32.980
and then I called her.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.223
And I was parked in her parking lot,

00:08:36.120 --> 00:08:38.681
but I had a backdrop that looked

00:08:38.681 --> 00:08:40.480
like she couldn't tell what it was.

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:41.910
And I started talking to her-

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:42.870
You green screened it?

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:44.120
I didn't green screen it, no,

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:47.020
I was like, I was
against a white building,

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:48.660
but it was just white.

00:08:48.660 --> 00:08:49.510
You couldn't tell.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:51.540
Well, did she say, where are you?

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.022
I said that I was just getting out of a-

00:08:53.022 --> 00:08:55.180
studio way.

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:56.013
I was just getting out-

00:08:56.013 --> 00:08:56.846
Of a meeting in my car, so I was...

00:08:56.846 --> 00:08:58.860
As she could tell, I was outdoors

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.280
in a parking lot.

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:01.601
Okay.
I couldn't hide that.

00:09:01.601 --> 00:09:03.551
And I didn't wanna show a sprinter van.

00:09:04.549 --> 00:09:07.420
And, but I was asking her about her exam.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:08.253
And then I was like,

00:09:08.253 --> 00:09:09.750
"Listen, have you ever gotten a package?

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:11.270
'Cause mom told you the package

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:12.103
is coming tomorrow."

00:09:12.103 --> 00:09:14.257
And I start walking up
there and she's like,

00:09:14.257 --> 00:09:16.280
"Well, typically it comes to the mailbox,

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:18.440
but mom's saying that
they're gonna deliver

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:19.273
it to the dorm."

00:09:19.273 --> 00:09:20.680
And I'm like, "Yeah, I think,

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:24.240
it's gonna show up somewhere around here."

00:09:24.240 --> 00:09:25.610
And I turned around and I showed

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:27.600
the sign to her dorm.

00:09:27.600 --> 00:09:29.000
And she freaked out.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.091
Mm-hmm.

00:09:30.091 --> 00:09:31.220
And then, she came outside

00:09:31.220 --> 00:09:34.754
