01:09:49.390 --> 01:09:51.883
We haven't written
Christians off in our lives,

01:09:53.390 --> 01:09:55.203
and still taught regularly to many.

01:09:57.150 --> 01:09:59.460
And I do think that for those

01:09:59.460 --> 01:10:03.120
who are truly reformed, sort of like all

01:10:03.120 --> 01:10:07.040
the way to full tulip Calvinists.

01:10:07.040 --> 01:10:07.873
Yeah.

01:10:10.250 --> 01:10:12.230
I know that they're worried about us,

01:10:12.230 --> 01:10:13.560
but then, I think that they have

01:10:13.560 --> 01:10:16.100
the ability to kind of farm it out to,

01:10:16.100 --> 01:10:18.040
well, if they're not
chosen, they're not chosen

01:10:18.040 --> 01:10:19.600
and I have to deal with that.

01:10:19.600 --> 01:10:21.370
But it's not like I can say much

01:10:21.370 --> 01:10:23.233
to change them at this point.

01:10:26.110 --> 01:10:27.390
I think, the way that I'm beginning

01:10:27.390 --> 01:10:31.483
to think about belief in convincing people

01:10:31.483 --> 01:10:32.316
and that kind of thing.

01:10:32.316 --> 01:10:34.320
Again, I have this, I
wanna convince people

01:10:34.320 --> 01:10:36.630
of things, but you start realizing

01:10:36.630 --> 01:10:39.340
that no one ever has been ever,

01:10:39.340 --> 01:10:40.480
no one's ever been forced

01:10:40.480 --> 01:10:41.751
into believing something.

01:10:41.751 --> 01:10:46.580
Believing something is
an involuntary reaction

01:10:46.580 --> 01:10:48.520
to a set of circumstances,

01:10:48.520 --> 01:10:50.960
and experiences, and predispositions.

01:10:50.960 --> 01:10:53.040
You get to this place and you just,

01:10:53.040 --> 01:10:54.760
you either do believe that something

01:10:54.760 --> 01:10:56.110
is true, or you don't believe

01:10:56.110 --> 01:10:57.320
that something is true.

01:10:57.320 --> 01:10:59.310
Now, new information can be given to you

01:10:59.310 --> 01:11:01.670
that might make you reconsider it,

01:11:01.670 --> 01:11:05.810
but just the idea that I can say

01:11:05.810 --> 01:11:06.860
something that's going

01:11:06.860 --> 01:11:08.070
to fundamentally change the way

01:11:08.070 --> 01:11:09.610
somebody thinks about something,

01:11:09.610 --> 01:11:11.550
I'm actually moving more into that place.

01:11:11.550 --> 01:11:12.910
Not from a reform perspective,

01:11:12.910 --> 01:11:14.200
'cause I don't believe in that,

01:11:14.200 --> 01:11:15.340
but just from a...

01:11:19.610 --> 01:11:20.993
Don't worry too much about it.

01:11:20.993 --> 01:11:22.480
Like when you talk about,

01:11:22.480 --> 01:11:23.730
oh, well, I've said all this stuff

01:11:23.730 --> 01:11:24.740
that could be used against me.

01:11:24.740 --> 01:11:25.750
I know you're not really worrying

01:11:25.750 --> 01:11:26.583
about it, but-

01:11:26.583 --> 01:11:27.654
Yeah, I, I don't think-

01:11:27.654 --> 01:11:29.380
But you know-

01:11:29.380 --> 01:11:30.820
Will read any of that, or...

01:11:30.820 --> 01:11:35.540
I have, I've seen the
posts and the comments,

01:11:35.540 --> 01:11:37.610
and the reposts, and the soundbites,

01:11:37.610 --> 01:11:38.610
and all that stuff.

01:11:38.610 --> 01:11:42.220
And my mind has changed about those things

01:11:42.220 --> 01:11:43.110
over time to a place, it's like,

01:11:43.110 --> 01:11:45.140
well, of course, that's
what you're gonna say.

01:11:45.140 --> 01:11:46.050
Right.

01:11:46.050 --> 01:11:48.300
But as you talk about therapy

01:11:48.300 --> 01:11:51.923
and you talk about medication,

01:11:54.110 --> 01:11:56.763
I'm reminded of chapter two in this book,

01:11:57.700 --> 01:11:59.460
which I think was the most relatable

01:11:59.460 --> 01:12:01.840
for me, from Ian Harbor.

01:12:01.840 --> 01:12:04.050
Because Ian went through

01:12:04.050 --> 01:12:06.060
a deconstruction and went and moved

01:12:06.060 --> 01:12:08.840
to basically progressive Christianity.

01:12:08.840 --> 01:12:09.810
Okay.

01:12:09.810 --> 01:12:12.650
He mentions our friend, Science Mike.

01:12:12.650 --> 01:12:13.483
Oh, he does?

01:12:13.483 --> 01:12:15.543
What's the title of the chapter?

01:12:17.140 --> 01:12:19.470
"Progressive Christianity
Was Even Shallower

01:12:19.470 --> 01:12:21.960
Than the Evangelical Faith I Left."

01:12:21.960 --> 01:12:23.890
Right, and so, it was this idea of like,

01:12:23.890 --> 01:12:25.400
my faith was deconstructed

01:12:25.400 --> 01:12:27.238
and I moved into progressive Christianity.

01:12:27.238 --> 01:12:30.890
And what I found is
that they weren't giving

01:12:30.890 --> 01:12:33.730
me anything to build, to rebuild a faith.

01:12:33.730 --> 01:12:36.130
And also, it was characterized by

01:12:36.130 --> 01:12:38.920
a lot of rigid fundamentalist thinking,

01:12:38.920 --> 01:12:40.350
group think in this,

01:12:40.350 --> 01:12:41.940
that was stuff that I was uncomfortable

01:12:41.940 --> 01:12:43.480
with in the original thing that I left.

01:12:43.480 --> 01:12:44.490
Yeah.

01:12:44.490 --> 01:12:45.960
I find it interesting that the application

01:12:45.960 --> 01:12:46.793
was to go back

01:12:46.793 --> 01:12:49.210
to the original faith, versus just saying,

01:12:49.210 --> 01:12:52.010
I don't want to identify with an ideology,

01:12:52.010 --> 01:12:53.100
or a group thing.

01:12:53.100 --> 01:12:56.950
But progressives had become just

01:12:56.950 --> 01:12:58.980
as fundamentalist as the fundamentalist

01:12:58.980 --> 01:13:00.390
that they despised.

01:13:00.390 --> 01:13:02.120
Only now, instead of the litmus test

01:13:02.120 --> 01:13:04.740
being traditional values, it was wokeness.

01:13:04.740 --> 01:13:06.590
If you didn't tow the party line

01:13:06.590 --> 01:13:07.900
of progressive orthodoxy,

01:13:07.900 --> 01:13:10.540
you were an outcast, a heretic.

01:13:10.540 --> 01:13:11.630
I'd heard about the dangers

01:13:11.630 --> 01:13:14.160
of moralistic therapeutic deism, MTD.

01:13:14.160 --> 01:13:15.610
The default American religion

01:13:15.610 --> 01:13:16.850
in which God simply wants you

01:13:16.850 --> 01:13:18.860
to live a decent life, not be sad.

01:13:18.860 --> 01:13:20.990
And he doesn't intrude on your life.

01:13:20.990 --> 01:13:22.790
I originally ran a
progressive Christianity

01:13:22.790 --> 01:13:24.530
to counter that kind of shallow belief,

01:13:24.530 --> 01:13:27.080
but what I found was more of the same,

01:13:27.080 --> 01:13:28.680
only with new definitions.

01:13:28.680 --> 01:13:31.380
Wokeness was the new morality, therapy

01:13:31.380 --> 01:13:33.220
was the new path to happiness.

01:13:33.220 --> 01:13:35.700
Cancel culture was the
new church discipline.

01:13:35.700 --> 01:13:37.890
And like MTD, there was conveniently

01:13:37.890 --> 01:13:39.740
no personal God to place demands on

01:13:39.740 --> 01:13:41.310
your life in any meaningful way.

01:13:41.310 --> 01:13:43.480
And this progressive MTD,

01:13:43.480 --> 01:13:44.930
Elizabeth Gilbert's trope

01:13:44.930 --> 01:13:46.300
is the only thing left.

01:13:46.300 --> 01:13:48.400
God dwells within you as you.

01:13:48.400 --> 01:13:49.470
There's no way to distinguish

01:13:49.470 --> 01:13:52.450
between ourselves and
God, in this paradigm,

01:13:52.450 --> 01:13:53.663
we are God.

01:13:55.430 --> 01:13:56.263
He goes on to talk about,

01:13:56.263 --> 01:13:58.400
he's not anti-wokeness, or anti-therapy.

01:13:58.400 --> 01:14:00.670
He was in therapy for a couple years

01:14:00.670 --> 01:14:03.130
in college, can benefit many of us.

01:14:03.130 --> 01:14:04.100
But I think that-

01:14:04.100 --> 01:14:06.530
Therapy is the path to happiness?

01:14:06.530 --> 01:14:10.950
Well, maybe I would say that,

01:14:10.950 --> 01:14:13.040
okay, you've taken this opportunity

01:14:13.040 --> 01:14:16.300
to give your spiritual update,

01:14:16.300 --> 01:14:19.520
which kind of becomes
also a therapy update.

01:14:19.520 --> 01:14:21.513
So, how do you respond to that?

01:14:22.740 --> 01:14:24.523
Is therapy your religion?

01:14:26.020 --> 01:14:26.853
Definitely.

01:14:30.300 --> 01:14:34.070
I see therapy as my...

01:14:35.650 --> 01:14:39.713
I need therapy to help me
make sense of all this.

01:14:41.710 --> 01:14:42.930
I'm talking about,

01:14:42.930 --> 01:14:44.690
I've talked for over an hour

01:14:44.690 --> 01:14:46.810
and I'm just scratching the surface

01:14:46.810 --> 01:14:48.640
of insight into myself.

01:14:48.640 --> 01:14:51.360
This is the work that I'm doing

01:14:51.360 --> 01:14:56.060
is to understand my past, my present

01:14:56.060 --> 01:14:57.340
so that then, I can move

01:14:57.340 --> 01:15:01.446
into my future unburdened

01:15:01.446 --> 01:15:06.446
from unnecessary burdens.

01:15:07.716 --> 01:15:08.700
And be the...

01:15:10.390 --> 01:15:12.713
To love, I'm gonna go back to that.

01:15:12.713 --> 01:15:15.190
I mean, that is my goal,

01:15:15.190 --> 01:15:18.300
but I need professional help

01:15:18.300 --> 01:15:22.100
to understand myself and to break down

01:15:22.100 --> 01:15:24.730
the lies that I've been telling myself

01:15:24.730 --> 01:15:27.460
so that I will be free to be

01:15:29.680 --> 01:15:31.810
the best me I can be.

01:15:31.810 --> 01:15:34.842
Insert whatever trope
you want at that point.

01:15:34.842 --> 01:15:35.842
You know?

01:15:36.960 --> 01:15:39.633
I think that this is a path forward.

01:15:41.376 --> 01:15:42.430
It is not...

01:15:42.430 --> 01:15:43.440
It's not a religion.

01:15:43.440 --> 01:15:44.880
It's not something that I worship.

01:15:44.880 --> 01:15:49.880
It's not a system of beliefs, or actions.

01:15:54.524 --> 01:15:58.880
It's help, it's treatment in a lot of ways

01:15:58.880 --> 01:16:02.540
that then opens me up
to where I can go next

01:16:02.540 --> 01:16:05.940
on my life journey and spiritual journey.

01:16:05.940 --> 01:16:08.480
But I feel like I'm very much,

01:16:08.480 --> 01:16:10.280
everything that I've described today

01:16:11.410 --> 01:16:16.410
is I feel like I'm being held back

01:16:16.730 --> 01:16:20.000
from not fully processing my past.

01:16:20.000 --> 01:16:20.833
Mm-hmm.

01:16:20.833 --> 01:16:25.790
And this is my treatment to process it

01:16:25.790 --> 01:16:28.750
so that I can continue to move forward.

01:16:28.750 --> 01:16:33.000
To be, I wanna be open.

01:16:33.000 --> 01:16:34.230
I wanna be...

01:16:36.950 --> 01:16:39.000
I want to have a vibrant experience.

01:16:39.000 --> 01:16:40.820
I wanna live life to the fullest

01:16:40.820 --> 01:16:43.580
and I wanna make the most positive impact

01:16:43.580 --> 01:16:47.883
I can make while I'm here.

01:16:51.380 --> 01:16:54.860
And I think that this is a necessary step

01:16:54.860 --> 01:16:55.860
of treatment for me.

01:16:58.950 --> 01:17:00.670
I could, I guess, I could imagine

01:17:00.670 --> 01:17:02.860
that some people would
just worship therapy

01:17:02.860 --> 01:17:04.347
as a religion, but I...

01:17:06.400 --> 01:17:08.300
I just see it a lot simpler than that.

01:17:10.300 --> 01:17:11.490
I mean, the thing that I would say

01:17:11.490 --> 01:17:15.940
to a guy like Ian is I think,

01:17:17.760 --> 01:17:21.863
we're all on a journey toward wholeness.

01:17:23.130 --> 01:17:26.330
Well, if we're getting healthier,

01:17:26.330 --> 01:17:30.440
if we're seeking things
that will be a benefit.

01:17:30.440 --> 01:17:33.129
I don't wanna be on a
journey to wholeness.

01:17:33.129 --> 01:17:35.240
Yeah, right, right, right.

01:17:35.240 --> 01:17:38.070
When it's like, okay,
I've got it figured out,

01:17:38.070 --> 01:17:41.080
or this is when it's negative this

01:17:41.080 --> 01:17:42.640
and negative that, I'm against this,

01:17:42.640 --> 01:17:43.720
I'm against that.

01:17:43.720 --> 01:17:44.553
And so, I mean,

01:17:44.553 --> 01:17:46.350
I hear what he's saying when it's like,

01:17:46.350 --> 01:17:47.880
if you just move from being against

01:17:47.880 --> 01:17:48.880
a bunch of...

01:17:48.880 --> 01:17:51.080
Being against a bunch of other ,

01:17:52.160 --> 01:17:55.670
it's like, some people get off on that,

01:17:55.670 --> 01:17:56.660
but that's just not me.

01:17:56.660 --> 01:17:58.600
So, I guess I agree with...

01:17:58.600 --> 01:17:59.520
I feel that.

01:17:59.520 --> 01:18:00.790
Well, I mean, I definitely agree

01:18:00.790 --> 01:18:03.870
with the idea that fundamentalist thinking

01:18:03.870 --> 01:18:05.440
happens in multiple circles, right?

01:18:05.440 --> 01:18:06.602
We talked about

01:18:06.602 --> 01:18:07.435
that last time.
Yeah.

01:18:07.435 --> 01:18:08.268
And I'm very uncomfortable

01:18:08.268 --> 01:18:09.440
with a lot of the fundamentalist thinking

01:18:09.440 --> 01:18:11.093
that I see on the left, I am,

01:18:12.320 --> 01:18:14.040
because I think, there's not a lot of room

01:18:14.040 --> 01:18:16.670
for people to ask questions.

01:18:16.670 --> 01:18:17.610
Yeah.
Without being labeled

01:18:17.610 --> 01:18:19.510
and right, and there's a very binary way

01:18:19.510 --> 01:18:20.774
of approaching a lot of things.

01:18:20.774 --> 01:18:21.607
Mm-hmm.

01:18:21.607 --> 01:18:23.220
But, and obviously I believe

01:18:23.220 --> 01:18:24.780
that exists on the right and it was one

01:18:24.780 --> 01:18:26.440
of the things that I was
happy to leave behind.

01:18:26.440 --> 01:18:27.690
Not the reason I deconstructed,

01:18:27.690 --> 01:18:29.230
but just something I was happily,

01:18:29.230 --> 01:18:31.150
I was happy to leave behind.

01:18:31.150 --> 01:18:32.550
But if we're all trying

01:18:32.550 --> 01:18:33.830
to move towards wholeness,

01:18:33.830 --> 01:18:35.100
and we're all trying to make sense.

01:18:35.100 --> 01:18:37.010
Like you say, make sense
of your experience,

01:18:37.010 --> 01:18:37.910
and make sense of your life.

01:18:37.910 --> 01:18:39.230
And ultimately, I don't wanna...

01:18:39.230 --> 01:18:40.870
I don't wanna say it's about

01:18:40.870 --> 01:18:41.960
a pursuit of happiness

01:18:41.960 --> 01:18:43.530
because that's a little too shallow,

01:18:43.530 --> 01:18:44.860
'cause I think that happiness is just

01:18:44.860 --> 01:18:46.840
a state of being that comes and goes,

01:18:46.840 --> 01:18:47.673
and you can't...

01:18:47.673 --> 01:18:49.580
You can't achieve some person that...

01:18:49.580 --> 01:18:50.770
We used to talk about joy

01:18:50.770 --> 01:18:52.560
being much more important than happiness

01:18:52.560 --> 01:18:55.483
as Christians, right?
Uh-huh.

01:18:56.360 --> 01:18:58.943
I think for Ian,

01:19:01.330 --> 01:19:04.660
in his journey toward wholeness,

01:19:04.660 --> 01:19:05.620
for whatever reason,

01:19:05.620 --> 01:19:07.040
because of his personality makeup,

01:19:07.040 --> 01:19:10.453
his circumstances, his background having,

01:19:11.500 --> 01:19:13.607
tying into some kind of traditional system

01:19:13.607 --> 01:19:14.930
and an idea that there

01:19:14.930 --> 01:19:18.100
is a more well defined source

01:19:18.100 --> 01:19:19.980
of this authority and this purpose,

01:19:19.980 --> 01:19:22.563
it's something that he's after.

01:19:23.900 --> 01:19:24.900
And it might be something that

01:19:24.900 --> 01:19:26.050
is at least for right now,

01:19:26.050 --> 01:19:29.640
required in his journey toward wholeness.

01:19:29.640 --> 01:19:30.990
I'm not gonna blame him for that.

01:19:30.990 --> 01:19:32.413
Again, I can't change the...

01:19:32.413 --> 01:19:36.000
He deconstructed, he got into

01:19:36.000 --> 01:19:38.840
what he calls progressive Christianity,

01:19:38.840 --> 01:19:40.800
and then saw some emptiness there

01:19:40.800 --> 01:19:42.030
and is going back to something

01:19:42.030 --> 01:19:43.410
that feels more well defined,

01:19:43.410 --> 01:19:44.600
or just fits the...

01:19:44.600 --> 01:19:47.960
His particular disposition better.

01:19:47.960 --> 01:19:48.793
Mm-hmm.

01:19:48.793 --> 01:19:50.930
And I think, that that's the thing

01:19:50.930 --> 01:19:52.670
that I'm trying to like...

01:19:52.670 --> 01:19:54.650
But that's not what you're after,

01:19:54.650 --> 01:19:55.590
that's not what I'm after,

01:19:55.590 --> 01:19:57.527
but we're also not after
the same thing, right?

01:19:57.527 --> 01:19:58.507
Right, yeah.

01:19:58.507 --> 01:20:00.191
And so, to go back to your Randy Travis

01:20:00.191 --> 01:20:03.870
of it all; whereas, maybe if I was in

01:20:03.870 --> 01:20:07.303
that van coming down the highway,

01:20:08.290 --> 01:20:09.720
yeah, I'd listen to some Randy Travis,

01:20:09.720 --> 01:20:10.750
but I'm not gonna listen to Randy Travis

01:20:10.750 --> 01:20:11.583
the whole time.

01:20:11.583 --> 01:20:13.290
I'm gonna put on this book

01:20:13.290 --> 01:20:15.910
about some other thing
that I'm interested in.

01:20:15.910 --> 01:20:18.580
And that's my moving towards wholeness,

01:20:18.580 --> 01:20:19.975
and that's actually
following my intuition.

01:20:19.975 --> 01:20:22.600
And in that case, it's following my desire

01:20:22.600 --> 01:20:25.970
that my intuition tells
me is good for me, right?

01:20:25.970 --> 01:20:26.803
Yeah.

01:20:26.803 --> 01:20:27.636
Versus like, I'm gonna do something

01:20:27.636 --> 01:20:29.030
that's gonna tear down me

01:20:29.030 --> 01:20:30.980
and tear down my relationships and-

01:20:30.980 --> 01:20:32.053
Right, right.

01:20:33.106 --> 01:20:33.939
And to me,

01:20:33.939 --> 01:20:38.850
and this sounds whatever, woo, whatever,

01:20:38.850 --> 01:20:41.203
that's spirituality broadly defined.

01:20:43.210 --> 01:20:44.650
It doesn't have to have...

01:20:44.650 --> 01:20:47.230
It doesn't have to be super well defined

01:20:47.230 --> 01:20:50.123
because I'm not able to define it well,

01:20:51.990 --> 01:20:53.480
and that's not something I'm after.

01:20:53.480 --> 01:20:54.480
And I don't think it's something

01:20:54.480 --> 01:20:55.580
that you're after.

01:20:55.580 --> 01:20:56.413
Yeah, right.

01:20:56.413 --> 01:20:59.520
But if that's something
that you are after,

01:20:59.520 --> 01:21:01.240
you are going to gravitate

01:21:01.240 --> 01:21:03.250
towards orthodox systems.

01:21:03.250 --> 01:21:04.490
And you know what, maybe

01:21:04.490 --> 01:21:06.740
that's what's best for you at this point,

01:21:06.740 --> 01:21:08.850
And I'm not gonna try to
convince you otherwise.

01:21:08.850 --> 01:21:12.160
Yeah, okay, well, we'll end it there.

01:21:12.160 --> 01:21:15.530
I think, it was...

01:21:15.530 --> 01:21:17.880
I've got some more bones to dig up.

01:21:17.880 --> 01:21:19.591
I'm gonna be digging up bones for a while.

01:21:19.591 --> 01:21:20.424
Mm-hmm.

01:21:20.424 --> 01:21:22.010
That's a Randy Travis reference,

01:21:22.010 --> 01:21:23.220
I know you're catching that.

01:21:23.220 --> 01:21:24.880
But I will leave you with a wreck

01:21:25.841 --> 01:21:30.841
and I'm gonna stay in an audio book

01:21:32.010 --> 01:21:32.843
that I've been listening

